{"version" 2 "boxes" [{"id" "madp_ga_lead" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "ga · run me" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 40.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "madp_ga_lead_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nGA: interactive evolution, after Karl Sims. Each tile is a little program run once per pixel,\nand you are the fitness function: click two tiles and they become the parents of the next\ngeneration. A child copies one parent, sometimes borrows a few words from the other, and\nmutates. Reroll breeds again from the same parents; Fresh Parents starts from noise.\n\nThe language is reverse Polish: every word takes its inputs off a stack.\n  x y          position, 0..1 (y grows downward)\n  r a          distance from the centre, angle around it (both 0..1)\n  rgb hsl      three numbers -> a colour\n  sat hue lum  set one part of a colour\n  + - * /      numbers, or colours channel by channel (wrapped into 0..1)\n  sin cos tan asin acos atan exp ln invert normalize   change one value\n  perlin       phase -> noise      fbm   phase lacunarity -> layered noise\n  dot          two values -> a number\n  a b c if     b when c > 0.5, else a\n  blend        a number and two colours -> the colours mixed\n  dup          copy the top\nAn empty stack reads 0.5 and unknown words are skipped, so every program draws something.\n\nThese two parents are the demo's starters. Edit them and run the box again (alt-R); the\nparents you pick are printed under the grid, ready to paste back in here.\n*/\nval ga = colorRpnEvolution(\n    \"\"\"\n    x 9 * sin 0.18 +\n    y 0.55 +\n    0.62\n    hsl\n    \"\"\",\n    \"\"\"\n    a 14 * cos 0.14 +\n    r 0.78 * 0.12 +\n    0.48\n    hsl\n    \"\"\",\n    ColorRpnBreeding(mutationRate = 0.12, targetLength = 18),\n)\n"}}} {"id" "madp_ga_fbm" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "fbm bands × noise hues" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 1240.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "madp_ga_fbm_code_.kt" "inline" "// Layered noise along a diagonal, and two noises in x and y added into a hue.\ncolorRpnEvolution(\n    \"x y + 7 * 2.2 fbm 0.65 0.55 hsl\",\n    \"x 6 * perlin y 9 * perlin + 0.5 * 0.7 0.55 hsl\",\n)\n"}}} {"id" "madp_ga_numbers" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "only the numbers mutate" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [800.0 1240.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "madp_ga_numbers_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nThe breeding rules are settings too. ColorRpnBreeding's weights say how often each kind of\nmutation happens (the demo's mix: num 33%, var 19%, op 20%, splice 10%, copy 6%, drop 6%,\nadd 4.5%, swap 1.5%). Here only numbers change and nothing is borrowed from the other\nparent, and nudgeLength = false stops the length being topped up with random words, so every\nchild keeps its parent's shape: the same rings and bands at different frequencies.\n*/\ncolorRpnEvolution(\n    \"r 12 * sin a 9 * cos + 0.6 0.5 hsl\",\n    \"x y + 7 * 2.2 fbm 0.65 0.55 hsl\",\n    ColorRpnBreeding(\n        mutationRate = 0.25,\n        seedSplice = 0.0,\n        weights = mapOf(\"num\" to 1.0),\n        nudgeLength = false,\n    ),\n)\n"}}} {"id" "madp_ga_noise" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "noise mask × rings" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [800.0 40.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "madp_ga_noise_code_.kt" "inline" "// Two of the demo's example programs as parents: a perlin mask blended with its own\n// inverse, and rings crossed with spokes.\ncolorRpnEvolution(\n    \"x 8 * perlin dup invert 0.3 blend\",\n    \"r 12 * sin a 9 * cos + 0.6 0.5 hsl\",\n)\n"}}}] "persistentProperties" ["frame" "name" "code" "code_language" "contents_language" "default_property" "file_proxy_mode" "file_proxy_path" "file_proxy_original_path" "file_proxy_mime" "filename" "preamble" "introduction" "attic" "notes" "geometryReviews" "geometryAppearance" "fragment" "stackSL" "rectSL" "msl" "vertex" "vertex_fragment" "task" "mesh" "raygen" "miss" "closesthit" "anyhit" "intersection" "callable" "fragment_s" "vertex_s" "task_s" "mesh_s" "raygen_s" "miss_s" "closesthit_s" "anyhit_s" "intersection_s" "callable_s" "children" "parents" "compute" "compute_s" "customization" "source_id" "templateId" "_tombstone" "isRemoteJSRoot" "isPythonRoot" ".*_editorState" "metadata" "nested" "nestedIn" "playlist" "pauseList" "bookmarks" "drawing" "panes" "slideShow" "autorun" "layers" "layerFrames" "_controlGroupValues" "keyframeData" "keyframeInterpolants" "ai4_auto_name" "ai4_auto_name_signature" "ai4_chat_history" "ai4_chat_running" "ai4_chat_suspension" "ai4_session" "fileManagerAccessHistory" "kitRole"]}